3. Typed comparison (read the JS, filemanager.html:474-596).
   Comparator `cmp(a,b,column)` (lines ~486-512):
     - name: localeCompare with sensitivity:'base', numeric:true.
     - rows / size: `(parseInt(av,10)||0) - (parseInt(bv,10)||0)` — integer
       comparison, NOT string. `data-size` is the raw int64 byte count
       (template line 1377: `data-size="{{.Size}}"`, and Size is
       models.FileInfo.Size int64 = info.Size() bytes, loader.go:718). The
       rendered `(25K)` cell (line 1384) is `div(.Size,1024.0)` rounded, so
       25K=25600 bytes sorts above 4K=4096 bytes correctly by byte count.
     - enabled: parseInt 0/1.
     - mindate: empty string → Infinity; `an===Infinity` → r=1 (a after b);
       then `r * dir`. Ascending (dir=1): empty sorts last. Descending
       (dir=-1): empty sorts first. Matches the brief's "last in ascending"
       rule. Non-empty mindate is ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` (loader.go:703
       `minD.Format("2006-01-02")`), so lexical `<` = chronological. ✓
   Sort target: `tbody.querySelectorAll('tr[data-name]')` — the empty-state
   colspan row (lines 1406-1410) has no data-name and is correctly skipped,
   so it is neither reordered nor dropped.

4. Sort survives htmx swaps (HIGH-RISK item).
   - Swap sources confirmed in the template:
     * upload form (line 12): hx-target="#file-list" hx-swap="innerHTML".
     * enable/disable checkbox (line 1393): hx-target="#file-list"
       hx-swap="innerHTML".
     * per-row delete (line 1397): hx-target="#file-list" hx-swap="innerHTML".
     All three replace the innerHTML of `<div id="file-list">` (line 211),
     which wraps the `filemanager-file-list` template (line 212).
   - Persisted state: the IIFE `window.FileManagerSort` holds
     `state = { column, direction }` in its closure (line ~478). This closure
     lives on `window`, OUTSIDE the swapped `#file-list` region, so it
     survives every innerHTML replacement.
   - Re-apply: `document.body.addEventListener('htmx:afterSettle', ...)`
     (line 594) calls `FileManagerSort.reapply()` → `wireButtons()` →
     re-binds header buttons (guarded by `dataset.sortBound==='1'` to avoid
     double-binding) and, if `state.column` is set, calls `applySort()` to
     reorder the freshly swapped rows. Confirmed via filemanager.html:594-596
     and the `wireButtons` body at lines ~570-584.
   - The listener is attached to `document.body`, which is NOT inside
     `#file-list` and is never swapped by any of the three hx-targets above.
     The script block itself sits at line ~474, outside `#file-list` (which
     closes at line 213), so the listener registration is not destroyed.
   - `renderIndicators()` re-sets `aria-sort` and arrow state on the rebuilt
     `<th>` elements after a swap, so the indicator also survives. ✓

5. Accessibility (vs ACCESSIBILITY.md numbered baseline).
   - A-4 / A-5 Keyboard + visible focus: each sortable header is a real
     `<button type="button" data-sort-btn="...">` inside the `<th>`
     (filemanager.html:1340-1368). No bare-`<th>` click handler. Button
     class includes `focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2
     focus-visible:ring-indigo-500` — a visible focus ring in both themes
     (indigo-500 is visible on white and on gray-900). Click handler bound
     via addEventListener in `wireButtons`, not via an inline `onclick=`.
   - A-7 Real table semantics: every `<th>` carries `scope="col"`
     (lines 1338, 1346, 1354, 1362, 1370). The structure remains
     `<table>/<thead>/<tbody>/<tr>/<td>`, no div grid.
   - A-9 Never color-only: `renderIndicators()` sets
     `th.setAttribute('aria-sort', state.direction==='asc' ? 'ascending'
     : 'descending')` on the active header and `th.removeAttribute('aria-sort')`
     on the others (lines ~537-551). Sort state is programmatically
     determinable, not conveyed by the arrow glyph alone.
   - A-8 Icons: the arrow span has `aria-hidden="true"`
     (filemanager.html:1343, 1351, 1359, 1367). It is decorative; the
     accessible name comes from the button text ("File"/"Rows"/etc.).
   - A-2 Both themes: header classes include `dark:` variants; the
     `focus-visible:ring-indigo-500` ring renders in both light and dark
     (Tailwind `focus-visible:` is theme-independent). Arrow glyph is
     text content using the button's `text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400`
     color, visible in both. ✓
   - A-14 CSP-clean: no inline event-handler attributes; behavior attaches
     from the inline `<script>` via addEventListener. (The repo's existing
     pattern uses inline `<script>` blocks; no new external origin.)

